    {
     "line": "WELCOME TO THE OFFICE OF THE PRESIDENT",
     "position": "college_ceo",
     "window": [
      "Getting to Mendocino College",
      "Public Information Office",
      "50th Anniversary",
      "WELCOME TO THE OFFICE OF THE PRESIDENT",
      "Mendocino College takes pride in being a community college with outstanding academics and exceptional support programs. We provide education opportunities at our Ukiah Campus, Lake County Center, North County Center, Coast Center, online, and in partnership with many local school districts. Our purpose is to provide you with a world-class education so that you can achieve your dreams.",
      "I find myself reflecting with gratitude on the college’s half a century of service to the students, families and communities of our region. For more than 50 years, Mendocino College has helped people build careers, transfer to universities, explore new interests and strengthen our local communities. That commitment remains at the heart of everything we do.",
      "Mendocino College serves a vast and diverse area. We are one of eleven California Community College Districts to be designated as rural-serving. The geographic, demographic, and economic realities of rural-serving institutions are unique from our suburban and urban peers."
     ],
     "emails": []
    },
